.Dd March 30, 2026
.Dt HTPM2TOOL 1
.Os HEIMDAL
.Sh NAME
.Nm htpm2tool
.Nd TPM 2.0 utility for attestation, enrollment, and key management
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar command
.Op Ar options
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a command-line tool for TPM 2.0 operations.
It supports attestation workflows (Safeboot-style enrollment),
encrypted envelope sealing to remote TPMs, quote generation and
verification, and signed timestamp creation.
.Pp
.Nm
uses the
.Xr libhtpm2 3
library, which communicates with TPMs directly via
.Pa /dev/tpmrm0 ,
Unix sockets (for
.Xr swtpm 8 ) ,
TCP, or pipes.
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Cm timestamp
Generate or verify a signed timestamp for use as qualifying data
(nonce) in TPM quotes.
The timestamp prevents replay of old quotes.
.Pp
The timestamp format is 44 bytes:
key version (4 bytes, big-endian uint32),
Unix time (8 bytes, big-endian uint64),
HMAC-SHA-256 of the version and time (32 bytes).
.Pp
To generate:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
htpm2tool timestamp --key keyfile [--key-version N] --out timestamp.bin
.Ed
.Pp
If
.Ar keyfile
does not exist, a random 32-byte HMAC key is generated and written
to it.
The default key version is 1.
.Pp
To verify:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
htpm2tool timestamp --key keyfile --verify timestamp.bin
.Ed
.Pp
The key version is read from the timestamp.
If
.Fl -key
is a directory, the verifier loads
.Pa <dir>/v<version>
as the HMAC key, enabling key rotation.
If
.Fl -key
is a single file, it is used regardless of version.
.Pp
Prints the decoded time and key version if the HMAC is valid;
exits non-zero otherwise.
.It Cm encrypt-to
Encrypt a file to a target TPM using the EncryptTo protocol.
The plaintext is encrypted using Encrypt-then-MAC: AES-256-CBC
with HMAC-SHA-256 over the IV and ciphertext.
The encryption and MAC keys are derived from a random master key
via KDFa.
The master key is split into 1\(en3 XOR shares, each wrapped via
MakeCredential to the target's Endorsement Key (EK).
.Pp
.Bd -literal -offset indent
htpm2tool encrypt-to \\
    --ek-pub ek_pub.bin \\
    --policy policy.bin \\
    --in plaintext \\
    --out ciphertext \\
    --cred-out creds \\
    [--iak-name iak_name.bin] \\
    [--owner-name owner_name.bin]
.Ed
.Pp
Options:
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Fl -ek-pub Ar file
Target TPM's EK public area (TPMT_PUBLIC, binary).
Compatible with
.Xr tpm2_readpublic 1
.Fl o
output and
.Xr tpm2_createek 1
.Fl u
output.
.It Fl -policy Ar file
Policy digest (32 bytes) to enforce on the well-known key share.
.It Fl -in Ar file
Plaintext input file.
.It Fl -out Ar file
Ciphertext output file.
Format: IV (16 bytes) || AES-256-CBC ciphertext (PKCS7 padded) ||
HMAC-SHA-256 (32 bytes).
Encryption and MAC keys are derived from the master key via KDFa.
.It Fl -cred-out Ar prefix
Output prefix for credential files.
Produces
.Ar prefix Ns .wk.blob ,
.Ar prefix Ns .wk.secret ,
and optionally
.Ar prefix Ns .iak.blob ,
.Ar prefix Ns .iak.secret ,
.Ar prefix Ns .owner.blob ,
.Ar prefix Ns .owner.secret .
.It Fl -iak-name Ar file
Optional: IAK Name for identity-binding share.
.It Fl -owner-name Ar file
Optional: Owner hierarchy key Name for decommissioning share.
.El
.It Cm envelope-open
Decrypt an EncryptTo ciphertext using the local TPM.
Connects to the TPM, creates the necessary keys (EK, well-known key,
optionally IAK and owner key), runs ActivateCredential for each share,
reconstructs the AES-256 key, and decrypts.
.Pp
.Bd -literal -offset indent
htpm2tool envelope-open \\
    --transport socket:/path/to/tpm \\
    --policy policy.bin \\
    --cred-in creds \\
    --in ciphertext \\
    --out plaintext \\
    [--iak-pub iak_pub.bin --iak-priv iak_priv.bin] \\
    [--with-owner]
.Ed
.Pp
Options:
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Fl -transport Ar uri
TPM transport URI.
Supported schemes:
.Dq device:/dev/tpmrm0 ,
.Dq socket:/path ,
.Dq tcp:host:port ,
.Dq pipe:command .
.It Fl -policy Ar file
The same policy digest used during encrypt-to.
.It Fl -cred-in Ar prefix
Input prefix for credential files.
.It Fl -in Ar file
Ciphertext input.
.It Fl -out Ar file
Plaintext output.
.It Fl -iak-pub Ar file , Fl -iak-priv Ar file
Optional: IAK public and private blobs (loaded under SRK).
.It Fl -with-owner
Optional: include the owner hierarchy key share.
.El
.It Cm quote-verify
Validate a TPM quote and/or replay an eventlog against a PCR
extension database.
.Pp
.Bd -literal -offset indent
htpm2tool quote-verify \\
    [--quote quote.bin --signature sig.bin --ak-pub ak_pub.bin] \\
    [--nonce nonce.bin] \\
    [--eventlog eventlog.bin] \\
    [--db pcr_extensions.db] \\
    [--pcr-policy "0-7=validate,8=ignore,10=initial"]
.Ed
.Pp
Quote verification checks:
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
Magic value (0xff544347) and type (TPM_ST_ATTEST_QUOTE).
.It
Signature over the TPMS_ATTEST blob using the AK's public key
(RSA RSASSA or ECC ECDSA).
.It
Nonce (qualifying data) matches expected value.
.El
.Pp
Eventlog validation replays the TCG PC Client binary eventlog,
checking each PCR extension against the SQLite database.
Extensions can be marked
.Dq good ,
.Dq bad ,
or
.Dq unknown ,
with severity levels and expiry timestamps.
.Pp
PCR policy (command-line argument):
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Dv validate
Replay eventlog, check each extension against DB.
.It Dv initial
PCR must be unextended (all zeros).
.It Dv ignore
Skip this PCR.
.El
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Generate a timestamp nonce and use it to verify a quote:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
htpm2tool timestamp --key nonce.key --out nonce.bin
htpm2tool quote-verify --quote quote.bin --signature sig.bin \\
    --ak-pub ak_pub.bin --nonce nonce.bin \\
    --eventlog /sys/kernel/security/tpm0/binary_bios_measurements \\
    --db /etc/htpm2/pcr_extensions.db \\
    --pcr-policy "0-7=validate,8-9=ignore,10=validate,11-23=ignore"
.Ed
.Pp
Encrypt a secret to a remote TPM:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
htpm2tool encrypt-to --ek-pub target_ek.bin --policy boot_policy.bin \\
    --in secret.key --out secret.enc --cred-out enrollment
.Ed
.Pp
Decrypt on the target:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
htpm2tool envelope-open --transport device:/dev/tpmrm0 \\
    --policy boot_policy.bin --cred-in enrollment \\
    --in secret.enc --out secret.key
.Ed
.Sh INTEROPERABILITY
.Nm
uses the raw TPM marshalled format (TPM2B_PUBLIC, TPM2B_NAME) for
all key and name files.
This is the same format produced by Intel's
.Xr tpm2-tools 7
suite:
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
.Ic tpm2_readpublic Fl c Ar handle Fl o Ar pub.bin
produces a file compatible with
.Fl -ek-pub
and
.Fl -ak-pub .
.It
.Ic tpm2_createek Fl G Ar rsa Fl u Ar ek_pub.bin
produces a compatible EK public file.
.It
.Ic tpm2_readpublic Fl c Ar handle Fl n Ar name.bin
produces a Name file compatible with
.Fl -iak-name
and
.Fl -owner-name .
.El
.Pp
There is no dependency on
.Xr tpm2-tools 7 ;
.Nm
can produce all these files itself.
However, files from either tool are interchangeable.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr swtpm 8 ,
.Xr tpm2_quote 1 ,
.Xr tpm2_createek 1
.Sh STANDARDS
TCG TPM 2.0 Library Specification, Parts 1\(en4.
.Pp
TCG PC Client Specific Platform Firmware Profile Specification.
.Sh AUTHORS
The
.Nm
utility and the
